# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
# Symptom: file starts with a UTF-8 Byte Order Mark (BOM: EF BB BF in hex).
#   BOM causes the first chromosome name to be parsed as ï»¿chr1 instead
#   of chr1, causing "inconsistent naming convention" or "chromosome not found".
#   Arises from Excel/Notepad on Windows exporting UTF-8 with BOM.
chr1	100	200	feature001	0	+
chr1	300	400	feature002	0	-
